#: includes/abilities.php:276
msgid "This site holds a stored value for one of the requested references that cannot be read. This is a data condition on the site, not a problem with the request, so repeating the call unchanged will not help; the details are in the site error log. Other references are unaffected."
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: comma-separated rejected keys, 2: comma-separated accepted keys.
#: includes/abilities.php:435
#, php-format
msgid "Unknown input key: %1$s. This ability accepts: %2$s. A key it does not declare is never read, so the request would be answered as though that key had not been sent — on the filtering ability that means an unfiltered result set that looks like a filtered one."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:437
msgid "no input at all"
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: length of the submitted term in bytes, 2: the limit in bytes.
#: includes/abilities.php:609
#, php-format
msgid "The search term is %1$d bytes long; WordPress applies no search term over %2$d bytes and discards it inside the query without reporting anything. Shorten it and call again. The limit counts bytes, so accented characters and emoji cost more than one each."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:949
msgid "This ability takes no parameters. Call it with no input at all."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1008
msgid "The input has to be an object, for example {\"type\": [\"web-design\"], \"per_page\": 5}. Every parameter is optional; calling this ability with no input at all returns the first page of all listed references."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1342
msgid "The input has to be an object carrying an \"id\" property, for example {\"id\": 42}."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1362
msgid "The \"id\" parameter is required and names the reference to return. It is a reference post ID as returned by jpkcom-acf-references/query-references, not a title and not a slug."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1375
#: includes/abilities.php:1386
msgid "The \"id\" parameter has to be a positive whole number."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1400
msgid "That id does not resolve to a reference that can be read. The answer is deliberately identical for an id that does not exist, one that is not a reference, and one that is not publicly readable."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1510
msgid "Term slug. Use this value as filter input, never the name."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1514
msgid "Human-readable term name. Locale-dependent, and not valid as filter input."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1518
msgid "Number of posts carrying this term across the whole site. NOT narrowed by any other filter, so it does not describe the size of a combined result set, and it counts every post status the taxonomy is attached to."
